          "html": "<ul>\n<li>Ductile: strain-controlled, high energy, cup-and-cone, dimples in SEM</li>\n<li>Brittle: stress-controlled, low energy, flat cleavage, no warning</li>\n<li>DBT: BCC and HCP show it; FCC does NOT</li>\n<li>Charpy: qualitative only. T_t = 50% upper shelf energy. Fine grain → lower T_t</li>\n<li>Griffith: brittle only. σ_f = √(2Eγ/πa). Internal crack: a = half-length; edge crack: a = full length</li>\n<li>K = σ√(πa) (α = 1 for edge crack). Fracture when K ≥ K_IC</li>\n<li>K units: MPa√m; G units: J/m². K_IC² = EG_c</li>\n<li>σ_f ∝ 1/√a — doubling crack length reduces safe stress by √2</li>\n</ul>",
