      "numLabel": "Topic 6 of 7",
      "title": "Fatigue",
      "subtitle": "Fatigue is the most common cause of engineering fracture — responsible for 50–90% of all mechanical failures. A part can fail under cyclic loads far below its UTS, often with no visible deformation. The surface is everything in fatigue.",
